desc(
	mode: "source",
	language: "general",
	title: "Absolute URLs",
	title_zh: "检测到Absolute URLs",
	type: vuln,
	level: middle,
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-absolute-urls",
	risk: "Best-Practice",
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `absolute-urls` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/apex/lang/best-practice/ncino/urls/AbsoluteUrls.yaml).
Original message: Using absolute URLs to Salesforce Pages is bug prone. Different sandboxes and production environments will have different instance names (like "na10", "na15" etc.). Code using absolute URLs will only work when it runs in the corresponding salesforce instances. It will break as soon as it is deployed in another one. Thus only relative URLs, i.e. without the domain and subdomain names, should be used when pointing to a salesforce page.

CWE: -
References:
- 
Note: original paths.exclude ['*Test*', '*test*'] not applied (SF path filter limitation).
DESC,
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Follow the framework's secure configuration guidance; remove or replace the flagged pattern.
SOLUTION,
	alert_min: 1,
	"file://pos.cls": <<<POS
http://nZXvisualforce.com.................

POS,
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG,
)

${*.cls}.pattern_regex(/(http|https):\/\/.*(salesforce|force|visualforce)\.com\.*/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Absolute URLs",
	title_zh: "检测到Absolute URLs",
	message: "Absolute URLs",
}
